  "version": "2.0",
  "pipeline_stage": "validated",
  "title": "Brain criticality predicts individual levels of inter-areal synchronization (Fusca, Siebenhuehner, Wang et al., 2023): SEEG/MEG PLV and DFA (derivative)",
  "description": "This derivative dataset provides phase-locking value (PLV) connectivity and detrended fluctuation analysis (DFA) exponents computed from resting-state stereo-EEG recordings of 68 patients with drug-resistant focal epilepsy. It also includes group-level MEG wPLI/DFA results from 52 healthy participants and hierarchical Kuramoto model simulations. The data support the finding that brain criticality predicts individual levels of inter-areal synchronization. Raw recordings are not included.",
  "methods_description": "SEEG was recorded for 10 minutes of eyes-closed rest per patient. Epileptic artifact windows were removed and contacts were referenced to the closest white-matter contact. Signals were filtered and decomposed with 24 Morlet wavelets (2-225 Hz) to compute PLV between contact pairs and DFA exponents per contact. MEG was recorded in 192 eyes-open resting sessions, source-reconstructed to the 400-parcel Schaefer atlas, and analyzed with wPLI and DFA.",
